// OCHO - the TABLE half of the scene script.
//
// The rules live in the kernel above (`kernel`, pure). This half:
//   - seats the game (every occupied seat, clockwise; fewer than two = practice against bots),
//   - starts a match with the kernel and a setup (shuffle seed, first player),
//   - draws the kernel state on the table after every move: hands in the seats' real hand zones
//     (or a row by the seat in practice), the play pile on DiscardPile, the draw pile on Deck,
//   - takes moves from clicks, drags onto the pile and HUD buttons, plays the bots, and runs the
//     OCHO call / catch race (the one part of the game that is not turn by turn).
// Every module-level name here starts with "tx" so the kernel extractor never mistakes table code
// for a kernel helper.
// ============================================================================================

